  "goodToKnow": "Das Festland is the mainland, as opposed to islands: aufs Festland zurückkehren. Germany's North Sea islands like Sylt, Föhr and the East Frisian islands are reached from the Festland by ferry; Sylt also has a railway causeway, the Hindenburgdamm. Rügen in the Baltic is Germany's largest island, linked by bridge. The British call continental Europe der Kontinent. It has no plural."
